>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>New York probate law decides who inherits when there is no will, when a small estate can skip full probate, and who can sign a deed for an inherited house.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Spouse and issue: $50,000 and one-half of the residue to the spouse, balance to issue by representation. (EPTL \u00a7 4-1.1(a)(1); <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/EPT/4-1.1' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Spouse and no issue: the whole to the spouse. (EPTL \u00a7 4-1.1(a)(2); <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/EPT/4-1.1' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Issue and no spouse: the whole to the issue by representation. (EPTL \u00a7 4-1.1(a)(3); <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/EPT/4-1.1' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A small estate is one leaving personal property with gross value of $50,000 or less (excluding EPTL 5-3.1(a) set-off property); handled by voluntary administration. (SCPA \u00a7 1301; <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/SCP/1301' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in New York?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy New York houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-york-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>New York Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-york-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>New York Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-york-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/'>New York Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/new-york-guides-by-city-and-county/'>New York guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-new-york/'>We buy houses in New York</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/EPT/4-1.1' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>EPTL \u00a7 4-1.1(a)(1)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/SCP/1301' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>SCPA \u00a7 1301</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for New York Probate Laws, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with 