<span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>New York Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a New York Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales sale</li><li>Turn the New York Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a New York House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>When property tax goes unpaid in New York, the statutes allow the taxing authority to sell a lien or the property itself, and they give the owner a set time to redeem.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Redemption period expires two years after lien date; a tax district may lengthen it for residential or farm property, or shorten it to one year for vacant and abandoned residential property. (RPTL \u00a7 1110; <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/RPT/1110' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Persons with interests may file a claim under RPTL 1135 or Title 6 for a share of any surplus attributable to sale of a foreclosed parcel. (RPTL \u00a7 1136; <a href='https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/RPT/1136' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;